WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Controls and thermostats are the brain of the system. When they fail, nothing
works right.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Recovery and evacuation lab: recover refrigerant from a system using approved
equipment, weigh and record the amount recovered, perform a nitrogen pressure
test, evacuate to 500 microns, verify vacuum holds for 10 minutes, then recharge

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Here's why this matters on the job: This sequence — recover, repair, pressure
test, evacuate, charge — is the standard procedure for every major
refrigerant-side repair.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Watch out for these: Never skip the pressure test. And — Evacuation to 500
microns minimum

00:02:24.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

